/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 27 767 [
[(From this example onward we'll put scalars in their own separate window)]
[(\050"data02"\051 - this will allow us to use the name of the window to indicate)]
[(to [pointer] objects where to look for scalars to attach themselves to.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 28 865 [
[(The scalars in any particular window, such as "data02" here, are kept in a)]
[(particular order. The [pointer] and [vpointer] objects allow you to)]
[(iteratively scan through the scalars in order. Each [\050v\051pointer] can be)]
[(attached to some scalar, or can be unattached, or can be attached to the)]
[(beginning of a window before any of the scalars in it \050the "head"\051.)]
[(Different [pointer] objects might be attached to the same scalar, or not.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 37 322 [
[(The [get] object takes a pointer, checks that its structure agrees with)]
[(what [get] is expecting, i.e., "triangle01", and if so outputs the values)]
[(of x, y, and color in the usual right to left order. If the requested)]
[(structure is given as a hyphen \050"-"\051, any structure is allowed, although)]
[(the field names should still be defined for whatever pointer comes in.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 377 223 [
[(You can combi)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 232 136 [
[(<-- note that the values come out as a list to the)]
[(right-hand outlet \050the left-hand one sends out pointers.\051)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 171 104 [
[(A pointer sent in a message is an elementary Pd type)]
[(on a level with "float" and "symbol", but its true)]
[(value can't be printed or saved to a file.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
